d rename is a direct, evidence-backed one.\n        </description>\n        <canonical_example id=\"define-alias-central-symbol-rename\" qa_rule_id=\"define_alias\" severity=\"error\">\n            <bad_code>#define HSD_AudioGetAuxHeapSize AXDriver_8038E034\n\nsize = HSD_AudioGetAuxHeapSize();</bad_code>\n            <preferred_code>/* config/GALE01/symbols.txt */\n/* Rename .text:0x8038E034 from AXDriver_8038E034 to HSD_AudioGetAuxHeapSize. */\nsize = HSD_AudioGetAuxHeapSize();</preferred_code>\n            <why>\n                - A canonical rename belongs in central symbol metadata or direct references, not in a source alias.\n                - Perform the evidenced rename once instead of masking duplicate names with a define.\n            </why>\n        </canonical_example>\n        <qa_rules>\n            - define_alias\n        </qa_rules>\n    </standard>\n    <standard id=\"truthful-headers-and-includes\">\n        <description>\n            - When a body proves a signature, updating the owning header and removing UNK_RET/UNK_PARAMS is required; leaving a mismatched prototype is rejected.\n            - Established include style is required and require-protos checks must run when prototype or include surfaces change; there are no exceptions to declaring a symbol in its real owning header.\n        </description>\n        <canonical_example id=\"headers-include-proto-shim\" qa_rule_id=\"define_alias\" severity=\"error\">\n            <bad_code>#define __THPReadFrameHeader __THPReadFrameHeader_proto\n#define THPDec_80330158 THPDec_80330158_proto\n#include &lt;dolphin/thp/thp.h&gt;\n#undef THPDec_80330158\n#undef __THPReadFrameHeader\n\nstatic u8 __THPReadFrameHeader(THPFileInfo* info);</bad_code>\n            <preferred_code>#include &lt;dolphin/thp/thp.h&gt;\n\n/* dolphin/thp/thp.h owns the recovered signatures. */\nstatic u8 __THPReadFrameHeader(THPFileInfo*);\nu8 THPDec_80330158(THPFileInfo* info);</preferred_code>\n            <why>\n                - Macro-renaming declarations around an include hides a prototype conflict instead of fixing the owning header.\n                - Repair the owning header signature and include it normally instead of using macro/prototype shims around the include.\n            </why>\n        </canonical_example>\n        <qa_rules>\n            - extern_in_c\n            - bare_local_prototype\n            - shadowed_declaration\n            - define_alias\n        </qa_rules>\n    </standard>\n</decomp_standards>\n</worker-packet>\n\n<target-knowledge-card-v2 ref=\"target-knowledge-card-v2\">\n    <target_knowledge_card_v2 unavailable=\"true\" reason=\"No target history was found.\"/>\n</target-knowledge-card-v2>"

